  "reflectionText": "Job sat on the ash heap, lifted his face out of the dust, and said: I know that my Redeemer lives. The words went out toward a day he could not yet see. What is it to lift your face out of the dust and speak toward a day you cannot yet see, addressing someone whose face you have not yet been shown?",
